# spamd.alloweddomains — greylist pass-through list for spamd(8).
#
# On-box path: /etc/mail/spamd.alloweddomains.
#
# spamd greylists new senders and traps mail to destination addresses whose
# domain is NOT listed here (see spamd(8) GREYTRAPPING). List every domain we
# accept mail for, otherwise legitimate mail to kyriakon.net users would be
# trapped and the sender blacklisted.
#
# This tracked copy is the seed for a box that has none; it is not the whole
# list on a running box. scripts/deploy-mail.sh merges /etc/mail/mail_domains
# into the installed copy on every deploy, and the drain appends `@<domain>`
# when it provisions a body's group, so a body's domain lives only in the
# installed file. Do not install this file over the live one: that deletes the
# body's line and makes spamd trap its mail.
#
# NOTE: greylisting itself is switched on at the pf layer (divert-to), which is a
# propose-only change; the fragment, its rationale and the checks are in
# docs/planning/research/spamd-greylisting.md. This file is the data half, and it
# is safe to commit because it contains no secrets.

@kyriakon.net
